# ===========================================================================
# correction/
# ===========================================================================
correction/models/*
# ...except the deployed detector. This is how the HPC gets the model:
# 04_train_model.py copies it here after every training run, and the archive
# of every past model stays in detection/models/runs/ (which is ignored).
!correction/models/object_detection/
!correction/models/object_detection/best.pt

correction/archive/
correction/logs/
correction/testing/
correction/.venv/

correction/data/*
# ...EXCEPT the master locations file. It is the accumulated result of
# months of manual verification and the one artifact here that cannot be
# rebuilt from code, so it is tracked: git is its backup and its sync
# between machines. ~10 MB, single layer -- update_master_locations.py
# replaces the layer rather than appending, so the file does not grow.
# Git can't merge a binary: pull before closing a round, push right after.
#
# Each level has to be re-opened explicitly -- git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so "!correction/data/training/Updates.gpkg" alone
# would never be reached.
!correction/data/training/
correction/data/training/*
!correction/data/training/Updates.gpkg

# ...and the CWNS facility names (FACILITIES.txt, ~31k rows, public CWNS
# data). The review app has always read it locally; the correction pipeline
# needs it on the HPC for owner-name vs plant-name matching (2026-09-25).
# The other CWNS exports stay out.
!correction/data/cwns/
correction/data/cwns/*
!correction/data/cwns/FACILITIES.txt

# Scratch output from diagnostic and verification runs
correction/temp/

# ===========================================================================
# detection/
# ===========================================================================
detection/.venv/
detection/data/

# reconstruct_tile_metadata.py writes to "--out reconstructed", a RELATIVE
# path, so its output lands in whatever directory you happened to run it from.
# It is derived -- re-runnable from the tiles and labels on disk -- and
# committing it scatters copies at different paths depending on cwd.
#
# detection/pipeline/reconstructed/ is already tracked from an earlier run and
# stays that way; a gitignore rule does not untrack what is already in. This
# only stops NEW ones being picked up.
reconstructed/

# The YOLO training set, built by 03_prepare_dataset.py from data/tiles/ plus
# the Label Studio export. ~1.2 GB of NAIP imagery, regenerated from scratch
# every time the dataset is rebuilt, and only ever used on the machine that
# trains the model. It was committed by accident on 2026-09-22 and took the
# repository from 181 MB to 1.2 GB -- untracked again the same day.
detection/dataset_filtered/

# ===========================================================================
# review_app/
# ===========================================================================
# close_round rebuilds this from the tracked master every time it runs, so a
# committed copy is a multi-MB binary carrying nothing the master doesn't
# already have. The per-round verdict exports beside it ARE worth keeping --
# they are the audit trail of what a reviewer saw and decided, and cannot be
# regenerated once app.db moves on.
review_app/data/outgoing/training_locations.gpkg

# ===========================================================================
# docs/
# ===========================================================================
# Scratch HTML the PNG renderer writes on its way to the image
docs/img/_fig.tmp.html

# ===========================================================================
# Editors, notebooks, bytecode
# ===========================================================================
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.bak-*
Untitled*.ipynb
